{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ECC",
  "chapter": 11,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ECC.11.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.11.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Cast thy bread upon the waters: for thou shalt find it after many days.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.11.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.11.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Give a portion to seven, and also to eight; for thou knowest not what evil shall be upon the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.11.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.11.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If the clouds are full of rain, they empty ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "themselves",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon the earth: and if the tree falleth towards the south, or towards the north, in the place where the tree falleth, there it shall be.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.11.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.11.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that observeth the wind shall not sow; and he that regardeth the clouds shall not reap.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.11.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.11.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As thou knowest not what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the way of the spirit, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "nor",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the structure of the parts of conception in her that is with child: even so thou knowest not the works of God who maketh all.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.11.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.11.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the morning sow thy seed, and in the evening withhold not thy hand: for thou knowest not whether shall prosper, either this or that, or whether they both ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " alike good.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.11.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.11.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Truly the light ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sweet, and a pleasant ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thing it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for the eyes to behold the sun:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.11.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.11.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But if a man shall live many years, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " rejoice in them all; yet let him remember the days of darkness; for they shall be many. All that cometh ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vanity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.11.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.11.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Rejoice, O young man, in thy youth; and let thy heart cheer thee in the days of thy youth, and walk in the ways of thy heart, and in the sight of thy eyes: but know thou, that for all these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God will bring thee into judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.11.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.11.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore remove sorrow from thy heart, and put away evil from thy flesh: for childhood and youth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vanity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
